WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.741
Welcome to Boston Builds, a public infrastructure budget explorer.
This site helps Boston

00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:11.629
residents and neighborhood groups understand planned investments
and decide which questions to bring

00:00:11.629 --> 00:00:16.046
to budget hearings. Instead of reading a long budget document, you
can move

00:00:16.046 --> 00:00:21.699
from citywide totals to a particular project, compare
neighborhoods, and download the underlying

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:26.880
records. This demonstration follows that journey. The central
question is not simply how

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.297
much money is listed. It is which investment to follow, who is
responsible,

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.300
and what information residents should ask for next.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.549
The overview contains three hundred twenty five project records
from Boston's adopted fiscal

00:00:40.549 --> 00:00:45.378
twenty twenty seven through twenty thirty one capital plan. Their
lifetime budgets total

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:50.043
about four point four seven billion dollars. Reported spending is
about three hundred

00:00:50.043 --> 00:00:54.873
ninety four million dollars through fiscal twenty twenty five, and
seventy eight records

00:00:54.873 --> 00:00:59.921
are labeled in construction. These indicators measure different
things. A lifetime budget is

00:00:59.921 --> 00:01:04.531
not money already spent, and published status is not a live
construction inspection.

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:09.032
The notice below the indicators also flags a discrepancy: the
City's summary lists

00:01:09.032 --> 00:01:14.026
three hundred twenty one projects, while the downloaded table
contains three hundred twenty

00:01:14.026 --> 00:01:14.300
five.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.482
Now I select Dorchester in the neighborhood filter. The dashboard
updates to twenty

00:01:20.482 --> 00:01:25.584
five projects with about one hundred eighty four million dollars
in lifetime budgets.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:30.626
Department bars show how that selected investment is divided. The
map highlights the

00:01:30.626 --> 00:01:36.449
source neighborhood, and selecting another mapped neighborhood
would change the same filter. This

00:01:36.449 --> 00:01:41.731
map does not identify exact construction sites. The budget table
has neighborhood labels

00:01:41.731 --> 00:01:47.313
but no street addresses or coordinates. Citywide and multi
neighborhood projects are retained

00:01:47.313 --> 00:01:51.635
in the overall totals, but are not spread across the polygons.
Below the

00:01:51.635 --> 00:01:56.437
map, the status chart shows project stages, and the funding chart
separates City

00:01:56.437 --> 00:02:01.419
capital, other City funds, grants, and external funds. These
controls help narrow a

00:02:01.419 --> 00:02:04.300
question without hiding what each measure means.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.681
Next, I reset the filters and search for project identifier C C C

00:02:09.681 --> 00:02:14.312
two five one six five. This opens the Grove Hall Community Center
record

00:02:14.312 --> 00:02:19.201
assigned to Dorchester. Its published scope is to design and
construct a new

00:02:19.201 --> 00:02:24.090
community center based on a programming study. The record lists a
sixty five

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:29.879
million dollar lifetime budget, about three point two million
dollars spent through fiscal

00:02:29.879 --> 00:02:35.025
twenty twenty five, and an in construction status. It also
identifies the owning

00:02:35.025 --> 00:02:40.493
and managing departments and breaks down the funding. These
details support a precise

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:45.960
question: what is the next construction milestone, and when will
residents receive an

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:51.235
update? They do not establish a completion date. Closing the
details and exporting

00:02:51.235 --> 00:02:55.030
the filtered C S V gives residents a record they can use in

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.474
a meeting or examine in a spreadsheet.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.380
The comparison panel places two neighborhoods side by side. Here,
Roxbury has about

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:10.553
three hundred fifty seven million dollars in listed project
budgets, compared with about

00:03:10.553 --> 00:03:15.257
one hundred eighty four million for Dorchester. I can change the
first selection

00:03:15.257 --> 00:03:20.019
to East Boston and see its totals alongside Dorchester. These
comparisons use the

00:03:20.019 --> 00:03:25.781
complete snapshot, independently of dashboard filters. They are
not adjusted for population, asset

00:03:25.781 --> 00:03:30.719
condition, or resident need. Crucially, about half of all budgets
belong to citywide

00:03:30.719 --> 00:03:35.305
or multi neighborhood records. A larger local total therefore does
not prove a

00:03:35.305 --> 00:03:40.302
neighborhood receives a fairer share or better services. The
comparison is a starting

00:03:40.302 --> 00:03:44.300
point for asking who benefits, not a ranking of neighborhood
equity.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:50.690
The findings lead to three oversight priorities. Schools and
Public Works hold about

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:55.880
fifty four percent of lifetime budgets. Ask for quarterly cost and
milestone updates

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.884
on their largest projects. About fifty point five percent of
investment spans the

00:04:00.884 --> 00:04:07.310
city or multiple neighborhoods. Request service areas and
beneficiary information before comparing local

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:12.932
shares. Finally, sixty projects totaling about five hundred fifty
three million dollars are

00:04:12.932 --> 00:04:17.071
labeled new project or to be scheduled. Ask for a named owner,
next

00:04:17.071 --> 00:04:23.003
decision date, and engagement opportunity. These labels support
questions, not a conclusion that

00:04:23.003 --> 00:04:24.300
projects are delayed.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:32.788
The methodology links official sources, dates, definitions, and
known inconsistencies. Missing addresses, completion

00:04:32.788 --> 00:04:38.379
evidence, and outcome measures limit what we can conclude. The
GitHub repository includes

00:04:38.379 --> 00:04:42.588
the collected C S V, a one page methodology note, and a
reflection.

00:04:42.588 --> 00:04:47.552
The public site works on phones and computers. Choose a
neighborhood, inspect a

00:04:47.552 --> 00:04:53.080
project, and export a shortlist. Boston Builds makes public
investment easier to examine

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:58.609
while keeping uncertainty visible. Follow the accompanying links
to explore the site and

00:04:58.609 --> 00:04:59.300
repository.
